Package: frmtmb.ddm
Title: Drift-Diffusion Response Times for 'frmtmb' Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Alex", "Forrence", email = "alex.forrence@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9728-6337"))
Description: Adds the Wiener first-passage time family to 'frmtmb', for
    two-choice response time data. A noisy evidence accumulator runs
    between two boundaries and the response time is the first time it
    touches one; the drift rate, boundary separation, non-decision time
    and start point each take their own regression formula. The
    parameterization follows 'brms'. The density is the Navarro and
    Fuss (2009) pair of series, written in plain R so that it
    differentiates exactly on an 'RTMB' tape, with a smooth weight
    between the two series because a tape cannot choose between them on
    a parameter.
